WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.550
This used to be a city.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:05.640
Shops.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.730
Homes.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.540
This used to be Western Mosul......

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.519
The rubble is strewn with decaying bodies
and unexploded bombs.

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:19.130
Zarah Abdul Quader lived through the fighting.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:24.810
She and her family spent weeks under siege
in their home - directly opposite the famous

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.160
Al Nouri mosque.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.930
That's where IS fighters hid from the international
coalition.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:37.859
The coalition bombed the city around her.

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:39.440
Nothing and no-one was spared.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.890
There was death and bombs and explosions everywhere.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.239
It simply didn't stop.

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:46.129
It was awful.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:51.839
They fled, but with nowhere else to stay,
they soon had to return.

00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:56.440
Back to their ruined neighbourhood, to the
two rooms of their house which were still

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.440
intact.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.089
Now they rarely venture out - fear of the
munitions scattered all around them keeps

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:03.969
the family at home.

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:07.650
There are still loads of shells lying around.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.340
The house opposite was destroyed and they
found something there.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:18.840
A mortar grenade or something - and it hadn't
gone off yet.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:24.229
Explosives expert Mark Warburton has been
in many crisis regions - but he says Mosul

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:26.670
is something new.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:34.930
They've found many bombs, grenades, mortars
- and thousands of explosive booby traps that

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:39.350
IS left on their retreat.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:45.880
They've been very well built but on an industrial
scale.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.549
It's not sort of just getting a few people
to building them here and there.

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:57.009
This has been sort of an industry too, to
build them to this scale and this amount.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:59.000
This was Al Shifa hospital.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.320
It was a modern clinic.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.579
Until the IS turned it into their headquarters.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:12.920
The search and clearance team work through
it by hand, piece for piece, metre for metre.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.610
The UN Mine Action Service has 60 people in
Mosul.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:23.450
It's nowhere near enough
The IS hid explosives so well that if you're

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.110
not extremely careful, you don't see them.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:31.330
If someone goes in somewhere where we haven't
been yet, and doesn't look out very carefully,

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.700
they can get blown up.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:41.940
As more people return, it becomes more urgent
to clear the deadly explosives still hidden

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.570
in the debris - or at least to mark which
areas are safe.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:51.980
But none of this is happening fast enough
- the remnants of the bitter fight for Mosul

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.310
are all over the place.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.420
Because this area was ISIS's final stand.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.790
What we have found here is a lot of suicide
belts.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:08.830
This has been without a doubt the sort of
main threat here.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.030
This is what he's talking about.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.330
A suicide belt among the rubble.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:19.390
Atmo: If you move round the corner, if you
take everyone that way around the corner ?

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.080
We move out of the danger zone in case it
blows up.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.060
It's soon cleared...

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:29.190
The belt had been packed with metal ball bearings
to maximize damage.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:34.540
You can clear a street one day but then we're
going to back the next day because people

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.720
find things in their houses.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:36.940
They shouldn't move them.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.820
They do, and then we have to re-clear them.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.870
The UN estimates that the clean-up of Western
Mosul will take a decade.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:49.690
But the residents don’t want to wait that
long - they are eager to return to their homes.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:54.080
But every shovel of rubble risks setting off
a booby trap.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.760
Rebuilding their homes is fraught with hidden
danger.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.760
Zahrah says she's happy that people are coming
back to Western Mosul.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:08.960
She hopes that each returning family will
increase the pressure on the international

00:04:08.960 --> 00:05:10.430
community to help them rebuild

00:05:10.430 --> 00:08:14.690
the city.

